Negative control for the empty state after a FAILED collection read.

Drops the guard, so *Nothing here yet — there is nothing to show in this
collection* is drawn under the very notice saying the collection could not be
read: the surface asserts a collection is empty when it never got an answer,
which is what the forced `error-collection` preset put on screen.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the list-surface empty-state spec — the empty sentences are drawn only
for a read that came back.

diff --git a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue
